          "Capability negotiation is important because protocol support and optional features can evolve. Record the negotiated protocol version and the capabilities actually advertised by the peer. Do not infer support from a server name or from documentation written for a different release. Version compatibility should be tested in CI using the exact client and server versions that will be deployed.",
          "Discovery results are metadata, not permission grants. A tool description can help a model understand intended use, but descriptions are not a security policy. The host should maintain its own allowlist, input constraints, and approval rules for high-impact actions."
