          "Remote MCP deployments use HTTP-based transport patterns defined by the current protocol specification. Older examples may refer to an SSE transport design that has since evolved, so verify the exact protocol revision and SDK version before copying configuration. Remote connectivity introduces network concerns such as TLS validation, authentication, authorization, request limits, and availability.",
          "Transport selection should follow the trust boundary. A local server is not automatically safe, and a remote server is not automatically unsafe. Ask which machine executes the tool, what credentials it can access, which users can connect, how requests are authenticated, and how the host revokes access."
