          "Recovery should be bounded. If a target disappears, take a fresh observation and re-plan once or twice rather than repeating the same click indefinitely. If the application enters an unknown state, stop and report what was observed. Never respond to uncertainty by escalating to broader permissions or issuing destructive fallback commands.",
          "Use idempotent operations where possible. For example, set a checkbox to a known state after reading its current value instead of toggling blindly. For file operations, check the destination and use safe temporary files before replacing important data. Maintain an action journal so interrupted workflows can distinguish completed steps from steps that need verification."
