        "heading": "9. Performance diagnostics and reproducibility",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Benchmark windows Task Scheduler vs Cron: Advanced Workstation Automation Patterns with a repeatable workload and record CPU, memory, disk I/O, network activity, and handle counts where relevant. Compare cold and warm runs, and separate startup cost from steady-state work. Do not optimize from a single Task Manager snapshot.",
          "Capture the PowerShell edition and version, module versions, OS build, execution identity, and relevant configuration in diagnostic output. These details often explain why a script behaves differently on a developer workstation and a CI runner.",
          "Use ETW or performance counters when process-level metrics are insufficient. Collect only the providers and duration needed for the investigation, protect trace files because they may contain sensitive operational details, and document how to reproduce the capture."
        ]
