          "Use bounded queues and reject or defer excess work with a clear response. Unbounded queues turn overload into growing latency and memory pressure. Expose queue depth and oldest-message age so operators can see when the system is falling behind.",
          "Apply circuit breakers or concurrency limits to dependencies that fail repeatedly. Recovery should be gradual to avoid a thundering herd when a downstream service returns. Keep retry budgets coordinated across every layer."
