        "heading": "2. Choose the right boundary for work",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A maintainable design for building True Offline Web Applications with Service Workers and Cache Storage assigns work to the environment best suited to it. Server-side work can protect secrets and reduce client computation; browser-side work can improve responsiveness and support offline behavior; edge execution can reduce geographic latency but may have runtime and API constraints.",
          "Keep component boundaries explicit. Avoid moving work to another runtime without accounting for serialization, network hops, caching, memory limits, and failure behavior. The fastest architecture is usually the one that avoids unnecessary work rather than the one with the most execution layers."
        ]
