        "heading": "5. Handle caching and lifecycle correctly",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Caching and lifecycle decisions are central to building True Offline Web Applications with Service Workers and Cache Storage. Define the cache key, freshness policy, invalidation event, and behavior when cached data is stale or unavailable. Treat user-specific data differently from public assets, and never allow a shared cache to serve one user's private response to another.",
          "Clean up event listeners, observers, workers, subscriptions, object URLs, and timers when their owner is no longer active. For offline or long-lived sessions, test version changes and interrupted updates. Resource lifecycle bugs often appear only after repeated navigation or extended use."
        ]
